 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S444-009\",\n \"clauses\": {\"create\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F02\", \"template\": \"Create a pattern that starts at {first_term} and uses the rule: {rule}. Which sequence shows this pattern?\", \"reasoning\": \"F02 opens with the imperative Create and asks the learner to identify the sequence that realises a pattern from a start value and an Add or Subtract rule. The selection format only approximates creating, but the family names the task directly.\"},\n  \"increasing_decreasing\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F02\", \"template\": \"Create a pattern that starts at {first_term} and uses the rule: {rule}. Which sequence shows this pattern?\", \"reasoning\": \"The rule slot is nested from F08, which prints Add or Subtract each time, so every problem states an increasing or decreasing rule. The declared bound is increasing_or_decreasing with identify_valid, which this family matches.\"},\n  \"patterns\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F03\", \"template\": \"Start at {first_term} and create {v} {pattern_label} with the rule: {rule}. Which pattern did you create?\", \"reasoning\": \"The pattern_label slot prints the object increasing pattern or decreasing pattern, so the object of the competency appears in the question. The same slot can also print repeating pattern, which is a fault recorded under failing_families.\"}},\n \"failing_families\": [\"F02\", \"F03\", \"F04\", \"F06\", \"F07\"],\n \"failing_templates\": [\"Create a pattern that starts at {first_term} and uses the rule: {rule}. Which sequence shows this pattern?\", \"Start at {first_term} and create {v} {pattern_label} with the rule: {rule}. Which pattern did you create?\", \"Start at {first_term} and use the rule: {rule_description}.\", \"Which sequence correctly shows {v} {pattern_label} starting at {first_term} and following the rule: {rule}?\", \"You want to create {v} {pattern_label} where the rule is: {rule}. Which sequence correctly creates it?\"],\n \"overall\": \"FAIL\",\n \"reasoning\": \"Fault 1, out of scope and contradictory: the pattern_label domain is a fixed list of three labels, including repeating pattern, and the generator chooses it independently of the rule. F03, F06 and F07 therefore can print text such as a repeating pattern whose rule is an Add or Subtract each time rule, which is outside this increasing or decreasing competency and internally inconsistent. Fault 2, grammar: v (a or an) and pattern_label are separate domains with no shared value, so the article need not match the label; the basis says the article follows the label, but the declared domains allow a mismatch in F03, F06 and F07. Fault 3, impossible sequences: first_term (1 to 3, 10 to 12, 15, 20, 30) and the rule (Add or Subtract, step 1 to 5, nested from F08) are independent domains, so a Subtract rule can start at a value that drives the sequence below zero within the six printed terms. A grade 2 Q2 learner cannot complete or check such a pattern. This affects F02, F03, F04, F06 and F07. The observed answer values (F09) and distractors (F10) show no negative numbers and no repeating-pattern text, so those families pass on what is shown; the faults above come from the declared domains. Vocabulary: sequence and rule are not in cumulative_vocab or NOT_YET_KNOWN, so they are not flagged as gate breaches. No family prints a NOT_YET_KNOWN term.\"}",
